Excerpt from evidence:4f01cfcf827adaa4b8ba0b8c35882ecf6cc623da3f293d49148714dd28404b74: Enhanced secondary analysis of survival data: reconstructing the data from published Kaplan-Meier survival curves

---

Very few authors [
7
] reported any assessment of their reconstruction of data. Earle [
] evaluated the reproducibility of using digitized software to extract the data by reporting an intraclass correlation coefficient. Parmar [
7
] calculated the ME on 48 studies between reconstructed HR using published survival curves and reconstructed HR using more direct estimates from either the Cox model or the logrank test results. He found no systematic bias for the HR and a slight systematic underestimation for their variance. We have provided a more complete evaluation of our method by reporting not only good reproducibility and lack of systematic error, but also information on MAE which tells us about the accuracy of the reconstruction that can be expected in a given instance.

---

Question: The cumulative recovery rate curves are in Fig. 2A of the original paper.

